1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,701
Can you show me storage:

2
00:00:06,701 --> 00:00:12,244
volumes, PersistentVolumes, PersistentVolumeClaims and StorageClasses?

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,727
A container's file system is temporary:

4
00:00:15,727 --> 00:00:20,230
when the container is replaced, everything it wrote is gone.

5
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:26,309
A volume is a folder that is mounted into the container and lives longer than it.

6
00:00:26,309 --> 00:00:26,984
emptyDir:

7
00:00:26,984 --> 00:00:32,913
a scratch folder that lives as long as the Pod; containers of the Pod share it.

8
00:00:32,913 --> 00:00:34,564
PersistentVolume (PV):

9
00:00:34,564 --> 00:00:38,091
a piece of real storage in the cluster (a disk,

10
00:00:38,091 --> 00:00:43,720
a network share, a folder on a node), which lives independently of any Pod.

11
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,821
PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC):

12
00:00:45,821 --> 00:00:48,823
a request for storage by an application:

13
00:00:48,823 --> 00:00:50,850
"I need 1 GiB, read-write".

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:58,059
Databases, uploaded files and queues must survive restarts, updates and node failures.

15
00:00:58,059 --> 00:01:04,252
Pods are disposable (lessons 08–09 replace them freely); their data must not be.

16
00:01:04,252 --> 00:01:07,117
PV and PVC separate the two concerns:

17
00:01:07,117 --> 00:01:17,570
developers ask for storage with a claim, without knowing whether it ends up on a cloud disk or a local folder; the cluster provides it.

18
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:21,753
And how does it actually work?

19
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,960
Static provisioning:

20
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:29,602
an administrator creates PVs by hand; claims bind to a matching one.

21
00:01:29,602 --> 00:01:31,345
Dynamic provisioning:

22
00:01:31,345 --> 00:01:39,477
the claim names a StorageClass (or uses the default one), and its provisioner creates a PV for it.

23
00:01:39,477 --> 00:01:47,443
This is the normal case in clouds (EBS, Azure Disk, Persistent Disk) and in Minikube (standard).

24
00:01:47,443 --> 00:01:48,522
Access modes:

25
00:01:48,522 --> 00:01:53,916
ReadWriteOnce (RWO, one node at a time, the usual for databases),

26
00:01:53,916 --> 00:02:00,140
ReadOnlyMany, ReadWriteMany (many nodes, needs shared storage such as NFS).

27
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:02,065
1.

28
00:02:02,065 --> 00:02:02,809
emptyDir:

29
00:02:02,809 --> 00:02:09,005
the writer appends the time every 5 seconds; the reader sees the same file.

30
00:02:09,567 --> 00:02:09,731
2.

31
00:02:09,731 --> 00:02:11,379
Static provisioning:

32
00:02:11,379 --> 00:02:15,086
a hand-made PV, and a claim that binds to it.

33
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:15,821
2.

34
00:02:15,821 --> 00:02:17,700
Static provisioning:

35
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:21,928
a hand-made PV, and a claim that binds to it.

36
00:02:21,928 --> 00:02:26,156
The claim asked for 500Mi and got the 1Gi PV:

37
00:02:26,156 --> 00:02:29,350
the smallest PV that satisfies it.

38
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:29,538
3.

39
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:34,088
The claim asked for 500Mi and got the 1Gi PV:

40
00:02:34,088 --> 00:02:37,102
the smallest PV that satisfies it.

41
00:02:37,102 --> 00:02:37,279
3.

42
00:02:37,279 --> 00:02:40,469
Dynamic provisioning and a database:

43
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:45,143
How do I see what Kubernetes did?

44
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,439
Where the data really is, on the Minikube node:

45
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,931
Let me try something.

46
00:02:52,931 --> 00:02:56,804
A claim for a StorageClass that does not exist:

47
00:02:57,367 --> 00:02:58,975
What should happen?

48
00:02:58,975 --> 00:03:01,007
The claim becomes Bound.

49
00:03:01,007 --> 00:03:02,192
What happened?

50
00:03:02,192 --> 00:03:07,271
It stays Pending, and a Pod using it would stay Pending too.

51
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:13,209
storageClassName cannot be changed on an existing claim:

52
00:03:13,209 --> 00:03:16,713
delete it and create it with an existing class.

53
00:03:16,713 --> 00:03:20,068
Here, the StorageClass of this lesson (keep):

54
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:22,547
Got it.

55
00:03:22,547 --> 00:03:25,298
What do I need to remember?

56
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:26,803
emptyDir:

57
00:03:26,803 --> 00:03:32,189
per Pod, temporary, shared between its containers.

58
00:03:32,189 --> 00:03:32,619
PVC:

59
00:03:32,619 --> 00:03:35,528
storage that outlives Pods.

60
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:44,701
Applications request storage with a PVC; a PV satisfies it, made by hand or by a StorageClass's provisioner.

61
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:46,372
Pending PVC:

62
00:03:46,372 --> 00:03:52,821
read its events (wrong class, no default class, nothing that matches).
